Acceptance:
1. Supervisor owns per-seat/per-generation ring under the runtime object directory. Fixed 56-byte little-endian version/kind/seat/generation/sequence/byte-offset/length/CRC32C header, raw output and typed resize/exit, compressed checkpoints. CRC32C test vector 123456789=e3069283. Header length bounded before payload allocation; marker reads capped at4097 bytes. Private0700 runtime directory; no ring content in repository/Git.
2. Records fsync before CRC-protected committed marker; marker and directory synced. Independent previous marker; fallback rejects torn/uncommitted suffix and reports recovered cursor. Suffix preserved as cold blob before truncation. Checkpoint-byte offset/capture cursor/generation checked before append. Full parser/UTF8/CSI/OSC/sync state and both screens preserved. Checkpoints after64KiB(default)+record boundary,200ms idle(default),resize/exit,or256 new records; replay also publishes intermediate checkpoints.
3. Active hot file default4MiB(setting), includes checkpoints/index/header. Compaction starts at a committed checkpoint, preserves at least newest two plus every following capture; older checkpoints stay while budget permits. Previous boundary can pin one more file of that size; temporary compaction file can add one more until publication. Retired/orphan hot logs go to zstd content-addressed cold blobs with cold.jsonl digest references. Cold is unbounded by the hot cap under never-delete. Metadata/index memory bounded by retained record count; no measured aggregate memory/performance claim.
4. Capture before live delivery; when detached, supervisor continues to committed ring without a per-seat memory backlog. It reserves checkpoint space and pauses PTY reads when no safe boundary exists. A restored logic publishes checkpoints while catching up, which makes eviction/capture resumable. Live test fills256KiB configured window while logic absent, observes paused status/unindexed tail, restores same child, drains655360+ bytes through to red AFTER-TAIL without a capture gap; older history has an explicit hot-eviction gap.
5. Ring recovery uses newest valid checkpoint plus bounded pages to an exact capture boundary. Playback uses fresh Term and drains generated effects without writing PTY responses, clipboard or messages. Generation-checked ReadRing/GetHistory returns records, optional logical indexes, next capture cursor and explicit requested/retained gap metadata. Logical row index counts LF/VT/FF and IND/NEL escapes outside OSC; resize, alternate, clear/reset advance epoch; no soft-wrap or guessed physical rows. Unparsed tail stays row:null until checkpoint/index publication.
6. Tests cover red SGR+4096 chars with red tail, incomplete CSI/UTF8/OSC and mode2026 checkpoints, replay/live cell equality, torn suffix rollback and subsequent append/reopen, checkpoint-boundary eviction with2+ checkpoints/cold copies,10k logical lines byte-for-byte paginated history, index epochs and unindexed tail, invalid generation/length/CRC and real live backpressure/restart/idle publication.

